---
/**
 * The /en/ Leaflet workaround. Scheduled for deletion in phase 5, when both
 * about pages load Leaflet from <head> and js/about.js loses its injector.
 */
---
    <!--Leaflet. On the Swedish page this sheet is fetched by js/about.js
        instead of being linked here, to keep 14kB of stylesheet for a section
        far below the fold off the critical path. That loader resolves
        'css/leaflet.css' and 'js/leaflet.js' relative to the document, so from
        /en/ it would look for /en/css/... and fail, hiding the map. Until the
        loader resolves those two paths from its own script URL, this page
        links Leaflet itself and loads leaflet.js ahead of about.js: about.js
        sees window.L already defined and goes straight to drawing the map.-->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/leaflet.css">
